# The DASHI integration / TOE spine

A single small spine that carries the corpus-wide cross-domain pass, rather than
a collection of per-domain reports.  Reading order:

1. `Integration.Levels` — the four-level classification (vocabulary, stored
   record dependency, shared implementation type, proved transport) as a Lean
   datatype, together with `Transport`, `NoTransport`, `Boundary` and `Socket`.
   Evidence constructors determine the level, so no row can be filed above the
   level it has a witness for.
